Fri Nov 06 10:45:00 UTC 2026 - Nicolas Morey <nicolas.morey@suse.com>

- Release 2.1
  - Privilege separation and process isolation:
    - Split daemon into supervisor and worker processes, dropping
      CAP_SYS_ADMIN and applying PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS in the worker
    - Require root execution, enforce non-writable source ownership,
      and scrub D-Bus and TSS2 environment variables
    - Enforce memory locking (mlockall) in production builds
  - Path traversal and filesystem security:
    - Harden path resolution using openat2 flags
    - Enforce nosuid, nodev, and noexec mount options, sanitize file
      mode bits, and reject unauthenticated POSIX ACLs in getxattr
  - Directory and inode handling:
    - Populate directory entry types in readdir to prevent lookup storms
      under GNU coreutils ls
    - Enforce bounded readdir buffers, robust offset tracking, and proper
      parent directory (..) inode resolution
  - Resource control and DoS mitigation:
    - Enforce per-UID open file tracking to prevent global exhaustion
    - Lower default worker thread count to avoid TPM hardware starvation
  - Audit subsystem overhaul:
    - Modularize audit subsystem with multi-ABI syscall monitoring,
      supervisor-worker socket isolation, rate limiting, and timeouts
  - CLI utility improvements:
    - Add atomic file creation and restrictive default permissions (0600)
      to cred-encrypt and cred-decrypt, with support for custom file modes

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Oct 16 07:45:00 UTC 2026 - Nicolas Morey <nicolas.morey@suse.com>

- Release 2.0
  - Switch to unified CRED_ENV v1 hybrid envelope encryption
    (RSA-OAEP-SHA256 + HKDF-SHA256 + AES-256-GCM) with per-file random
    keys and eliminate the shared <hostname>.key file
  - Bind the CRED_ENV v1 header, relative FUSE path, and POSIX file
    permissions (st_mode & 07777) into AES-256-GCM Additional
    Authenticated Data (AAD) to prevent ciphertext substitution and
    chmod tampering
  - Derive plaintext file size directly from the CRED_ENV v1 header and
    drop the user.size extended attribute requirement
  - Add cred-encrypt and cred-decrypt CLI utilities
  - Verify TPM public key attributes, pin the TPM object Name across
    decryptions, and add the tpm_pubkey mount option
  - Harden TCTI validation: scrub TSS2/TCTI environment variables,
    require /dev/tpmrm[0-9]+ for device TCTI, and restrict swtpm TCTI
    to test builds

